[30.7828, "o", "Help on VolumeService in module daytona._sync.volume object:\r\n\r\nclass VolumeService(builtins.object)\r\n |  VolumeService(volumes_api: 'VolumesApi')\r\n |\r\n |  Service for managing Daytona Volumes. Can be used to list, get, create and delete Volumes.\r\n |\r\n |  Methods defined here:\r\n |\r\n |  __init__(self, volumes_api: 'VolumesApi')\r\n |      Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\r\n |\r\n |  create(self, name: 'str') -> 'Volume'\r\n |      Create a new Volume.\r\n |\r\n |      Args:\r\n |          name (str): Name of the Volume to create.\r\n |\r\n |      Returns:\r\n |          Volume: The Volume object.\r\n |\r\n |      Example:\r\n |          ```python\r\n |          daytona = Daytona()\r\n |          volume = daytona.volume.create(\"test-volume\")\r\n |          print(f\"{volume.name} ({volume.id}); state: {volume.state}\")\r\n |          ```\r\n |\r\n |  delete(self, volume: 'Volume') -> 'None'\r\n |      Delete a Volume.\r\n |\r\n |      Args:\r\n |          volume (Volume): Volume to delete.\r\n |\r\n |      Example:\r\n |          ```python\r\n |          daytona = Daytona()\r\n |          volume = daytona.volume.get(\"test-volume\")\r\n |          daytona.volume.delete(volume)\r\n |          print(\"Volume deleted\")\r\n"]
